<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kyōgoku clan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kyōgoku clan was a Japanese warrior family, a branch of the Sasaki of Ōmi province. In the Muromachi period they served as shugo governors of northern Ōmi, Izumo, Oki and Hida, but in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku period</a> they lost power to their deputies, the Amago in Izumo and the Azai in Ōmi. The family recovered under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> and the Tokugawa, holding domains such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matsue">Matsue</a> and Marugame.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kyogoku-clan.jpg" alt="Kyōgoku clan" width="130" height="130" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 俊 (Shun Toshi) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kamon_yotumeyui.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
